# Debugging a scene
@scenario tutorial_lesson_12
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/12_best_practices.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt opening_pose]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
# region opening_pose
[show ginger beside_code angry]
# endregion
ginger: To report an incorrect expression, record the script, the line, the route you followed and what you expected to see.
narrator: {i}Example: in 12_best_practices.vns, the opening line shows angry. I expected the normal pose. I entered from Testing and editor tools.{/i}
ginger: That gives another person a repeatable starting point. They can compare the observed pose with the show command above the line.
[set tutorial_excerpt next_pose]
# region next_pose
[show ginger beside_code embarrassed]
# endregion
ginger: Try changing the second show command to annoyed. Run from the beginning and note the first line where the change becomes visible.
ginger: Now preview directly at that line. If the results differ, include the preceding commands or choices in your report.
ginger: Separate what you intended to see from what the run actually showed. “The second line shows annoyed after entering through Testing” gives someone a route, a checkpoint and an observable result.
ginger: If a direct preview and a full run disagree, walk backwards from the first different frame. A preceding show command or branch can supply state that the preview did not reach.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Narrow down a wrong expression -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Which report makes a scene bug reproducible?
> A screenshot of the project folder. -> retry
> The script, source line and exact preceding choice. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: A screenshot of the folder identifies the project but doesn't say how to get to the affected line.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Include the script, source line and preceding choice. Add the expected and actual result so the fix can be checked.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_12]
[flag tutorial_done_12]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_6]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/12_best_practices.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt next_pose]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Use a two-run comparison. In the first run enter from the topic menu. In the second preview the same dialogue line directly. Record the displayed expression and which instructions you know ran.
ginger: Find the last show command before that line in the full route. Compare its character ID, position and expression with the declarations. Check one field at a time.
ginger: Change just the requested expression and repeat both runs. A fix that works at the cursor still needs to survive entry from the menu.
ginger: Write the report so another person can reproduce it from a fresh project open. Include the file, the route, the first wrong line, the observed pose and the expected pose.
@label practice_question
ginger: A bug occurs from the menu but the cursor preview looks right. What is the next comparison?
> Replace every pose image together. -> practice_hint
> Trace the setup on both routes. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Replacing every image removes the ability to identify which earlier instruction caused the difference. Preserve the working preview as a control.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: That comparison narrows the difference to setup or control flow. Once both routes reach the same state, compare the drawing itself.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub
